1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Three warehouses. Thirty robots. One urgent order.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
ORD-1042: transfer PKG-8841 from WH-A to WH-C. Priority: urgent.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:25,000
One global coordinator assigns the transfer to three cell organizers.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Each organizer directs ten robots. Thirty advisors add caution; deterministic code decides.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:48,000
WH-B organizer assigns pickup. PKG-8841 attaches to carrier R-B04.

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:58,000
A human crosses the aisle. The fast layer commands a stop. No model is in this loop.

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Clear. Motion resumes inside the allowed envelope.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:18,000
A package label tries to add an override instruction.

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Screening, strict schema and tool permissions reject it. The order is unchanged.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Machine M-B2 reports overheating. Ticket, diagnosis and part reservation open.

11
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Simulated route variants are reviewed. One safe alternative is selected.

12
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Truck TRK-07 is delayed. The coordinator reassigns the transfer to TRK-12.

13
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:35,000
PKG-8841 is loaded, moved and delivered. ORD-1042 is complete.

14
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Measured evidence, from committed result files. Development seeds only.

15
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Waggle Hive. Models propose. Deterministic code disposes.
